{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '388,396p' paper.tex; sed -n '1,55p' global_memory_summary.md; tail -n 22 memory.md; sed -n '1,95p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py; ls global_memory/conclusions* 2>/dev/null; sed -n '1,45p' literature/Chen2026Strategic.opening.txt; cat literature/Faliszewski2009Bribery.abstract.txt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '388,396p' paper.tex; sed -n '1,55p' global_memory_summary.md; tail -n 22 memory.md; sed -n '1,95p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py; ls global_memory/conclusions* 2>/dev/null; sed -n '1,45p' literature/Chen2026Strategic.opening.txt; cat literature/Faliszewski2009Bribery.abstract.txt\"","aggregated_output":"\\subsection{Public snapshots, normalization, and reproduction map}\\label{sec:repro}\nThe Open LLM contents revision is\n\\begin{center}\\small\\texttt{9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2}.\\end{center}\nThe HELM source is the public bucket's MMLU release v1.13.0. The accompanying frozen resources retain upstream URLs, upstream byte checksums, original source-row indices, and known aliases. The acquisition code canonicalizes Unicode/whitespace and raw score content before split assignment. Raw content and known alias clusters are disjoint across the recorded split; unknown lineage is not covered by that check. HELM is already on a unit scale; Open LLM uses the published normalized columns divided by 100, without treating raw columns as additional tasks. This choice makes the response cap relative to the published task scale. A different nonlinear score calibration would define a different intervention problem.\n% @evidence[[data/openllm.json#/rows/0/provenance/0]]\n% @evidence[[data/helm.json#/rows/0/provenance/0]]\n% @evidence[[data/protocol.json#/normalization]]\n\n\\paragraph{Reproduction entry points.}\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-07 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected certified cap-response frontiers for mean versus ordinary median; status=idea_ready. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=No executed scientific finding or evaluated refinement justifies changing distilled conclusions.\n  - evidence: Bootstrap correct